+/// Render-target images are keyed by storage and shape, not format: the game
+/// reuses the same memory as different same-size formats within a frame
+/// (G-buffer RGB10A2 later read and written as RGBA8), so aliases must share one
+/// VkImage with per-format views. Key: pool, offset, texel class, w, h.
+using ImageKey = std::tuple<u64, u64, u32, u32, u32>;
